      "title": "[P1] Reset capability-backed updates after unkeyed cards",
      "body": "When a reused iframe already shows a live result whose snapshot capability was omitted, `capabilityChangesResult()` returns false for the next capability because the prior identity is null, while this fingerprint fallback is disabled whenever the new compatibility payload has a string capability. A different non-empty `openai:set_globals` result is therefore applied without `resetCurrentResult()`, allowing the previous card's `toolCallId` and view state to survive and potentially bind the new snapshot under the old card. Treat differing capability-backed payloads as a result boundary while preserving the identical split-delivery case.",
